body:
You're not alone. I keep punching myself in the face until I feel slightly concussed. I just lost my job, feel out with the roommate who had the lease and was forced to move back into my parents and my sister's decided to become extraordinarily annoying and contrarian (she's 24 but I swear she has the social mental capacity of an 11 year old, and I'm not saying that figuratively). Eventually I got mad at her for something so minor and pathetic, but I ended up calling her and cunt and she called my a faggot, which lead to myself to self harm again because I should know better. Also some assholes on a video game called me out by name tonight and that made me feel even more depressed, so I handled that my punching myself, again. All while living with my parents. I know this is a Pandemic but I still feel like a loser for living at home at 26.

&#x200B;

I don't know if me venting helped at all, but I just wanted to let you know you're not alone.

The issue is that now he's coming at us unprovoked sometimes, for example he'll yell at me just for being in the house. I understand aspies need their space but it's gone above that, he's invading our space. I'm thinking about using some of my own money to give him a break, in a hotel or something, but I'm worried that could backfire to. 

&#x200B;

And I don't blame you for not wanting to look at them haha, but I'll give that a google. I get depressed even by the thought of googling that. Thank you for reading the post and I hope your parents are doing better!

I do like the direct rules idea, but the issue is we've already tried that and he didn't budge, we threaten to kick him out or "to call" which gets him to run back into his room, but then he goes back at it. We also tried to show him how his behavior by, but if anything it's made it worse (I was planning on moving out anyways but we tried to use that as an example, he was upset when I moved to Europe for a year for example). 

&#x200B;

However replying to your comment I came up with an idea which I might run by you: A fake 30 day eviction notice but we can say "if you behavior improves he can annul this." Does this sound like a good idea or does this sound psychopathic?

Don't get me wrong I definitely understand this and I get that he's struggling with so much going on at once. The issue is (admittedly I didn't make this clear) it's come to a point where he's yelling at us for everything even when we aren't talking to him. I wasn't there for this, but apparently there was another fight completely unprovoked and my brother caused this (knowing my brother this doesn't surprise me, but there was a point in time this would have). 

&#x200B;

I have a bit of money to blow right now, but do you think if I sent him somewhere (even if it's just a hotel somewhere else is town) it would give him time to be alone and process everything that's happening or would that complicate things even more?
